{
  "assessment_scope": "Directory Design amendment only, with twelve relocated models, sixty-seven current example files and current governance/navigation interactions. Upstream accepted hierarchy-proposal-review and prior design-review inform preserved logical behavior; this review independently approves the new exact directory subjects and project-specific override.",
  "change_id": "2026-09-12-unified-validation-model",
  "contributors": [
    {
      "id": "root",
      "role": "design"
    }
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "id": "directory-design-review",
  "independence_basis": "Separately authorized reviewer agent assessed the author root's relocation and Design amendment without editing any Design, moved example, plan or implementation. Prior hierarchy assessment remains its own preserved subject-specific judgment.",
  "judgment": "approved",
  "limitations": [
    "Approval covers directory Design coherence, not completed reader implementation, runtime conformance, whole-initiative Code Review or Verify.",
    "Historical source/approval bytes are not retargeted; current renewed subjects are explicit. Root retains routing and implementation ownership."
  ],
  "rationale": [
    "System Repository directory layout explicitly declares all twelve model locations and the CLI Records and Skill Workflow example namespaces. Smaller logical children stay parent sections; stable model/requirement identities do not depend on filenames. This directly realizes the explicit user-selected physical tree without adding empty child folders.",
    "Design retains the portable matching-directory and historical-flat conventions and adds an exact repository-specific map. Unmapped nesting, model/example confusion, symlink targets and missing files still reject. Selectors must validate the actual owner for the moved example namespaces; historical deleted paths may route checks without becoming accepted present aliases.",
    "Independent pre-move comparison covers 79 model/example members. After resolving relocated Markdown destinations, only intended System/Design amendment prose differs; 50 JSON/Mermaid payloads are byte-identical and 311 comparable local link targets and anchors resolve to the same mapped obligations. Prior complete model semantic assessment remains applicable to unchanged logical contracts; changed layout provisions were directly read and assessed.",
    "Current model registration follows stable IDs and exact new paths; original review identities and historical artifact references are preserved rather than reinterpreted. Current navigation must resolve new owners while original paths in historical evidence continue to describe original subjects. No automatic governance adoption follows a move.",
    "Actual reader constraints are concrete: model validation currently admits flat/matching paths, selection derives old owner locations, and CLI fixture tests reference the old Records examples root. The approved amendment requires coordinated bounded repair and regression proof; author-reported new-path rejection is expected before that implementation and is not a defect in the selected Design.",
    "No product requirements, record JSON schema, public skill behavior, cache or executor implementation is selected. The associated bounded delivery plan supplies the reader migration and preservation checks. No material Design finding remains.",
    "Final runnable-example reassessment: CLI subject-inspection command now names docs/design/skill/workflow.md and docs/design/cli/records.md instead of removed locations. Directly inspected command retains its subject-inspection semantics and uses the approved owner map. This bounded source-navigation correction changes no transport, storage, synthetic JSON payload or product obligation. Current model/prose checks pass; exact CLI subject refreshed here, prior broader hierarchy review retains its original subjects."
  ],
  "reviewer": {
    "id": "proposal-reviewer",
    "role": "review"
  },
